---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="Enter a Quilt Cut List"
  description="Compile rectangular requirements quickly by keyboard or safe spreadsheet paste."
  eyebrow="Learn QuiltClarity · Cut requirements"
  guideSlug="enter-a-cut-list"
  guideCategory="start_here"
  previous={{
    href: '/guides/project-planner-tutorial/',
    label: 'Full Project Planner Tutorial',
  }}
  next={{
    href: '/guides/add-fabric-you-have/',
    label: 'Add Fabric You Already Have',
  }}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Prepare one row per repeated cut</h2><p>
      For each fabric, copy the piece label, quantity, width, height, and
      whether the pattern gives a Cut or Finished size. Add each project fabric
      before mapping rows to it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use the keyboard path</h2><p>
      Tab through a row and press Enter from its last editable value to add the
      next row. New rows inherit fabric and size mode for speed, but never hide
      or inherit dimensions. Duplicate similar rows, then edit the differences.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Paste tabular data safely</h2><p>
      Paste CSV or spreadsheet rows in <code
        >Fabric | Label | Qty | Width | Height | Size mode</code
      > order. Review the preview, resolve unmatched fabrics, and confirm. Malformed
      or ambiguous values never import silently.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use More options only when needed</h2><p>
      Set piece rotation, crosswise/lengthwise orientation, or WOF-strip
      behavior when the cut has a real constraint. Visible resolved cut-size
      feedback shows how Finished inputs use project seam allowance.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
